1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,900
Speaking Genie started with a personal problem.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,652
For years I kept taking

3
00:00:05,652 --> 00:00:09,200
courses to improve my English.

4
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:13,940
My grammar is good. I can write.

5
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:16,750
But when it comes to speaking… I'm lost.

6
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,800
I'm just not comfortable speaking.

7
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:22,087
It's not that I can't recall the words;

8
00:00:22,087 --> 00:00:23,980
I'm just not comfortable at all.

9
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:30,000
Then, when tools like LLMs and ChatGPT came out,

10
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:32,416
I started trying things myself,

11
00:00:32,416 --> 00:00:33,860
on my own devices,

12
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:36,060
trying out different ways to practise,

13
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:38,500
and I felt this could be an opportunity.

14
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,580
I showed the idea to my partner,

15
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,032
and together we thought about

16
00:00:43,032 --> 00:00:45,460
how it could help a lot of people.

17
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,100
And Speaking Genie was born.

18
00:00:51,895 --> 00:00:53,355
We're not a fixed course.

19
00:00:53,425 --> 00:00:55,132
We follow curricula,

20
00:00:55,132 --> 00:00:58,375
based on the framework you work with.

21
00:00:58,495 --> 00:01:01,151
We came up with the idea that you don't

22
00:01:01,151 --> 00:01:03,875
need to clear an hour in your schedule.

23
00:01:03,975 --> 00:01:06,475
Instead, you take short calls,

24
00:01:06,955 --> 00:01:11,275
each with a clear goal you practise on.

25
00:01:11,695 --> 00:01:14,675
And the other person isn't a real person.

26
00:01:14,935 --> 00:01:17,375
It's AI, so it's there 24 hours a day.

27
00:01:17,515 --> 00:01:19,806
We help you get comfortable:

28
00:01:19,806 --> 00:01:21,675
at first, you don't talk to real people.

29
00:01:22,175 --> 00:01:23,425
You talk to AI.

30
00:01:23,455 --> 00:01:26,575
And the AI doesn't judge you.

31
00:01:26,875 --> 00:01:29,395
It doesn't stop you mid-sentence,

32
00:01:29,425 --> 00:01:32,215
or say, "No, it's pronounced like this."

33
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:35,975
After every session, every call,

34
00:01:36,115 --> 00:01:39,215
you get detailed feedback on that call:

35
00:01:39,235 --> 00:01:40,941
what happened, what went well,

36
00:01:40,941 --> 00:01:42,875
what didn't, and what to improve.

37
00:01:43,135 --> 00:01:45,975
And you get feedback weekly and monthly.

38
00:01:46,535 --> 00:01:49,322
It's like the gym: the more you train,

39
00:01:49,322 --> 00:01:51,375
the better your level gets.

40
00:01:51,495 --> 00:01:54,215
Then it kept growing until it became a product,

41
00:01:54,235 --> 00:01:56,775
and now people come in and practise on it.
